essages  in this campaign unlike any other ross  lord  global news still ahead how french  satire  is striking back as a tragedy is put on  trial  [Music]  developments tonight in the case of the  man who inspired the hollywood film  hotel rwanda tonight paul  russo-savagina's family accuses rwanda's  government of kidnapping the 66 year old  on made-up charges rusa sabagena an  outspoken critic of rwanda's government  is now being held in rwanda's capital he  had traveled to dubai where he was  arrested on terror charges  rwanda's president holds close ties with  the united arab emirates  and has been accused of hunting down  critics overseas  in 1996 russo sabagena fled rwanda and  sought political asylum in belgium  in 2016 he announced a political  campaign against rwanda's government  which he labeled a dictatorship the  french satirical newspaper  charlie hebdo is republishing  controversial cartoons of the prophet  muhammad  as the trial for the deadly terror  attack on its paris office begins  the publication hasn't reprinted the  images since the aftermath  of the january 2015 attack which killed  several cartoonists the editors say we  have always refused to do so  not because it is prohibited the law  allows us to do so  but because there was a need for a good  reason to do it  a reason which has meaning and which  brings something to the debate  14 people are accused of being  accomplices in the shooting sprees  at the charlie hebdo offices and at a  kosher supermarket two days later  a total of 17 people died all three  gunmen involved were killed in shootouts  with police  the president of the philippines is  publicly ordering the country's top  customs official to shoot and kill  drug smugglers it's one of rodrigo  duterte's most overt threats yet  under his anti-drug crackdown he says he  fears narcotics are flowing into the  philippines through its ports  where corruption is deeply rooted more  than  5 700 mostly poor drug suspects  have been killed during duterte's  four-year anti-drug campaign  the focal point of his presidency  and north korea appears to be taking a  heavy-handed approach to cracking down  on the spread of covet-19.  leader kim jong-un has reportedly  ordered police and soldiers to shoot  anyone who gets within one kilometer of  the chinese border  the government is sending ammunition to  help officials carry out the new policy  which will be in effect until the  pandemic ends north korea claims to be  the only virus free country  in the world up next recognizing  canada's residential schools and their  place  in history  you're watching global national  the residential school system is a dark  chapter in canadian history  tens of thousands of indigenous metis  and inuit children  were forced to attend the government-run  institutions nearly 3 000 children are  known to have died  while at the schools it's likely many  other deaths were not documented  the abuse many experienced has affected  generations of families  today the federal government recognized  the system as a defining event that's  not to be forgotten  and as abigail beeman reports two former  schools  will now be national historic sites  that's where i slept  when he goes inside the former portage  la prairie manitoba residential school  now  ernie daniels smells chlorine five six  years old  all dragged up the stairs that way and  thrown into a  bathtub full of chlorine he grew up to  become  chief then successfully fought to  reclaim the building and surrounding  land  daniels calls the national historic site  designation  vindication we had a long road  winding road to this day former schools  in portage la prairie and schubernacher  nova scotia are now national historic  sites and the entire residential school  system is being declared historically  significant  as we recall the phrase to kill  the indian within the child for canada  to move forward and move forward in an  inclusive way and particularly with  indigenous p